            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for rust, then the Gujarati for to rust."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: સોની",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સોની — sonī — \"a goldsmith\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "અમારી ગલીમાં એક સોનીની દુકાન છે. amārī galīmā̃ ek sonīnī dukān che. There is a goldsmith's shop in our lane."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સોની (sonī) is built on the Gujarati word for gold, which goes back to Sanskrit suvárṇa, \"gold\" (CDIAL 13519). CDIAL also lists the older sonār, \"a goldsmith\", from Sanskrit suvarṇakāra (CDIAL 13520)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
