          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઓગાળવું (ogāḷvũ) goes back to Sanskrit avagalati, \"falls down, slips down\"; CDIAL lists the Gujarati verb for making something melt beside the plain verb for oozing and melting (CDIAL 742). The past agrees with what is melted: વીંટી ઓગાળી."
